
## Execute NeuroMTA Monitoring Server (optional)

Run `neuromta monitor` server with the command specified below. This command will automatically create a localhost server for monitoring simulation process.

```bash
neuromta_monitor_server     # run monitor server
```

```
usage: neuromta_monitor_server [-h] [--host HOST] [--port PORT] [--reload] [--access-log]

NeuroMTA Profiler Server

options:
  -h, --help    show this help message and exit
  --host HOST   Host address
  --port PORT   Port number
  --reload      Enable auto-reload
  --access-log  Enable access log
```

You can change several options with the predefined environment variables before attaching the client application to the monitor server.

```bash
export NEUROMTA_MONITOR_SIM_NAME=SIM_NAME   # the simulation (or client) name shown to the server
export NEUROMTA_MONITOR_HOST=127.0.0.1      # the monitor server IP
export NEUROMTA_MONITOR_PORT=8000           # the monitor server port
export NEUROMTA_MONITOR_TIMEOUT=1           # timeout for the client-server connection
export NEUROMTA_MONITOR_FREQ=0.5            # update frequency
```